Now we are all sitting here.
Asha, Rohan, Priya, and I are eating dinner.
Outside, it is still raining heavily.
But inside, there is great peace.
I look at my friends.
There is deep contentment in my mind.
I came to Mumbai in January.
Back then, I came here only for a job.
But in these six months, I have done so much more.
I have built a new life in Mumbai.
"Today's food is very tasty," Rohan says.
"Yes, this birthday celebration is wonderful," Priya says.
Asha laughs and looks at me.
"Maya, are you happy today?" Asha asks.
"Yes, I am very happy," I say.
Previously, I did not know this city.
But now I have found a family here.
Mumbai is now truly my home.
